## vast.ai benchmark configuration.
##   cp vast/.env.example vast/.env      # vast/.env is git-ignored — put secrets there only
##
## How to edit: lines starting with ONE "#" are settings showing their built-in default —
## remove that "# " to change one. Lines starting with "##" are explanations; they stay
## comments even if you strip one "#". Values with spaces must be quoted. No $expansion.
## Anything exported in your shell wins over this file:  MAX_HOURS=1 ./vast/bench.sh ollama
## Why each default was chosen: DESIGN.md.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- secrets (local)
## vast API key — or run `vastai set api-key <KEY>` once. VAST_API_KEY also works.
# VAST_AI_API_KEY=
## Optional Hugging Face token (HF_TOKEN also works). Forwarded to the instance, where it is
## visible in the vast console — use a read-only token.
# HF_KEY=

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- repo the instance clones
## Must be readable without credentials (public, or a URL with a token).
# REPO_URL=https://github.com/kashubianrodos/embeddings-test.git
## Default: your current local branch.
# REPO_BRANCH=

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- run control
## 0 = on-demand (default, both modes), 1 = interruptible bid: ~40% cheaper per hour but vast
## stops it whenever someone bids more or rents on-demand. CLI: --interruptible / --on-demand
# INTERRUPTIBLE=
## bid = min_bid × this
# BID_MULTIPLIER=1.25
## Preempted: wait this long (min) for a resume, then fetch logs + destroy.
# OUTBID_WAIT_MIN=5
## Running but no SSH this long (min) → fetch vast logs + destroy.
# SSH_WAIT_MIN=10
## Still loading (image pull) this long (min) → fetch vast logs + destroy.
# LOAD_WAIT_MIN=20
## Seconds; fetching logs can never block the destroy.
# FETCH_TIMEOUT=180
## Hard stop: fetch logs + destroy after this many hours, whatever the state.
# MAX_HOURS=3
## Refuse to rent if the cheapest offer's estimated run cost is higher ($).
# MAX_RUN_USD_OLLAMA=3
# MAX_RUN_USD_VLLM=6
## 1 = smoke-size benchmark (≈2 min). CLI: --quick
# QUICK=0
## 1 = don't ask before renting. CLI: --yes
# ASSUME_YES=0
## 1 = log every vastai call + output to vast/.debug.log (HF token redacted).
# VAST_DEBUG=0

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- offer ranking (total cost per run)
## est. cost = $/h × (download_GB×8000 / (inet_down × NET_EFFICIENCY) / 3600 + SETUP_HOURS + BENCH_HOURS)
##             + download_GB × inet_down_cost
## Share of advertised inet_down you really get (run_summary.md measures it).
# NET_EFFICIENCY=0.5
## Package install, engine start, model load — excluding the download (hours).
# SETUP_HOURS=0.1
# BENCH_HOURS_OLLAMA=0.75
# BENCH_HOURS_VLLM=1.5
## Minimum advertised download speed (Mb/s).
# MIN_INET_DOWN_OLLAMA=500
# MIN_INET_DOWN_VLLM=1000
## Skip hosts whose bandwidth costs more than this ($/GB).
# MAX_INET_DOWN_COST=0.02
# MIN_RELIABILITY=0.98
## Where the machine may be: europe (default: EU + UK, NO, CH, IS, LI, Western Balkans, MD, UA),
## eu (EU-27 only), any, or your own list of 2-letter country codes, e.g. "DE,PL,NL,CZ".
# REGION=europe
## Real network check ON the instance, before installing anything: download the first 200 MB of
## the model from Hugging Face. Below this (Mb/s) the host is replaced (advertised speeds lie).
# MIN_NET_MBPS=150
## During the model download: below this sustained rate (Mb/s, 5-min windows) the host is replaced.
# MIN_PULL_MBPS=80
## How many times a too-slow host is destroyed and replaced by the next cheapest offer.
# HOST_RETRIES=2
## vast machine_ids never to rent (comma list); slow hosts are added automatically during a run.
# EXCLUDE_MACHINES=
## Force one offer id (it must still pass the filters).
# OFFER_ID=
## Appended to the search query, e.g. 'machine_id!=137375'
# EXTRA_QUERY=

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- mode: ollama (GGUF: single-user feel + quality)
## Which model: q4k = Huihui-Qwen3.8-27B-abliterated Q4_K (16.8 GB, 24 GB card)
##              bielik-1.5b = speakleash Bielik-1.5B-v3.0-Instruct Q8_0 (1.7 GB, any ≥10 GB card)
## CLI: --preset bielik-1.5b. The OLLAMA_LLM_MODEL / _DISK_GB / _DOWNLOAD_GB / _GPU_NAMES lines below
## describe q4k only and are ignored for bielik-1.5b (LLM_MODEL=… still overrides any preset).
# OLLAMA_PRESET=q4k
## vast's SSH-mode base image; Ollama is installed on top at OLLAMA_VERSION.
# OLLAMA_IMAGE=vastai/base-image:stock-ubuntu24.04-py312-2026-09-07
# OLLAMA_VERSION=0.34.4
## Cards the ranker may pick from.
# OLLAMA_GPU_NAMES="RTX_3090,RTX_4090"
## Pin ONE card so speed numbers are comparable across runs, e.g. RTX_4090 (Ollama only;
## vLLM uses VLLM_GPU_NAME).
# GPU_NAME=
# OLLAMA_CUDA_MIN=12.4
# OLLAMA_DISK_GB=40
## model 16.8 + mmproj 0.9 + image 1.4 + Ollama ≈2 (GB)
# OLLAMA_DOWNLOAD_GB=22
## GGUF repo commit when this was written: 3f101cd22b7999228bbd5d79a33975414eb9758b
## (Ollama can't pin a revision; setup.log records what was pulled).
# OLLAMA_LLM_MODEL=hf.co/huihui-ai/Huihui-Qwen3.8-27B-abliterated-GGUF:Huihui-Qwen3.8-27B-abliterated-Q4_K.gguf
## Concurrent slots (each reserves KV cache), context, KV cache type (q8_0 halves KV memory).
# OLLAMA_NUM_PARALLEL=4
# OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH=8192
# OLLAMA_KV_CACHE_TYPE=f16

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- mode: vllm (serving capacity)
## fp8  = leoncca Mixed-FP8 (28 GB) on a 48 GB Ada/Hopper card (L40S, L40, RTX 6000 Ada, H100)
## bf16 = original BF16 (56 GB) on one 80 GB GPU — reference only
# VLLM_PRESET=fp8
## Pin one vLLM card, e.g. L40S (the preset's GPU query still applies).
# VLLM_GPU_NAME=
## v0.30.0-cuda-13.0 exists but needs driver ≥580 (fewer hosts).
# VLLM_IMAGE=vastai/vllm:v0.29.0-cuda-12.9
# VLLM_CUDA_MIN=12.9
## Preset-specific overrides. Leave these commented: the preset picks them. If you set one,
## it applies to BOTH presets. Defaults for fp8 (bf16 in the ## line under each).
# VLLM_LLM_MODEL=leoncca/Qwen3.8-27B-Huihui-Mixed-FP8
##   bf16: huihui-ai/Huihui-Qwen3.8-27B-abliterated
# VLLM_LLM_REVISION=3ea006fab18c94e486f446a874c15e25a02a0bd1
##   bf16: main
# VLLM_GPU_QUERY='gpu_ram>=45 compute_cap>=890'
##   bf16: 'gpu_ram>=79 compute_cap>=800'
# VLLM_DISK_GB=90
##   bf16: 130
## weights 28 + image ≈16 (bf16: 56 + 16 = 72)
# VLLM_DOWNLOAD_GB=44
## Server settings (both presets).
# VLLM_MAX_MODEL_LEN=16384
# VLLM_GPU_MEM_UTIL=0.92
## Empty = number of GPUs.
# VLLM_TP=
# VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS='--language-model-only --kv-cache-dtype fp8 --reasoning-parser qwen3'
